[0.326, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;78;186;101m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39m\u001b[1mUpdate\u001b[22m(~/projects/manifest.lane-c/docs/ships-plan.md)\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  \u001b[39mAdded \u001b[1m9\u001b[22m lines, removed \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m line\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 296 \u001b[22m   fly, the departure body's motion since its crossing ended, and, by the share flown, the arrival\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 297 \u001b[22m   body's motion still to come before the arrival crossing begins. At each end that is the crossing's\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 298 \u001b[22m   own place, so the frames join without a jump, and near each end the ship moves with that end's\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 299 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  body, which cannot catch it. Today's crossings are relative to the course's carrier, the star       \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 299 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  body, which cannot catch it.                                                                        \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 300 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m- **Checked, not assumed.** The blend keeps the course near its ends with the bodies, but at a low    \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 301 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  thrust share the pull towards the arrival body can bring a slow ship back inside a sphere while it  \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 302 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  still thrusts. So as a journey starts, `travel` samples the planned cruise each minute of its       \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 303 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  thrusting, against every sphere about each end's body where the bodies then are, each widened by    \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 304 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  a minute's travel at the ship's speed then. Where the drive would thrust inside one, it lengthens   \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 305 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  that end's crossing by the shortfall and plans again, at most `kClearanceRounds` (4) times, then    \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 306 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  refuses `InsideRadius` (a new result). `Policy::EstimateRoute` uses the clearances the check        \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 307 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  settles. Today's crossings are relative to the course's carrier, the star                           \r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[2m308\u001b[12G\u001b[22m  b\u001b[16Gtw\u001b[19Gen planets,\u001b[33Gich\u001b[37Gleaves a\u001b[46Gplane\u001b[52G's ship behind as it\u001b[73Gorbits on (about\u001b[90G250,000 km in\u001b[104Gthe 2.3\u001b[K\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m309\u001b[12G\u001b[22m  hours); the\u001b[26Ghaule\u001b[32G's 1,000 km crossin\u001b[52G and its\u001b[61Gcourse move to th\u001b[79Gse fra\u001b[86Ges too, and the W22a\u001b[K\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m310\u001b[13G\u001b[22m f\u001b[16Gxtures' pins move\u001b[34Gwith it.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B                                         \u001b[76G\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
