[0.381, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;78;186;101m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39m\u001b[1mUpdate\u001b[22m(~/projects/manifest.lane-c/docs/ships-plan.md)\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  \u001b[39mAdded \u001b[1m9\u001b[22m lines\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 321 \u001b[22m   crossings are relative to the course's carrier, the star between planets, which leaves a\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 322 \u001b[22m   planet's ship behind as it orbits on (about 250,000 km in the 2.3 hours); the hauler's 1,000 km\u001b[K\r\u001b[7C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m2\u001b[12G\u001b[22m \u001b[14Gcrossing \u001b[24Gnd it\u001b[30G course move to these frames\u001b[59Gtoo, and the W22a\u001b[77Gfixtures' pins move with\u001b[102Git.\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 324 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m- **Where it is settled.** `travel` runs the check as it admits the journey, docked, from the         \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 325 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  station's place at that step, to refuse early and to burn fuel for the settled course's driven      \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 326 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  metres (its length less the two crossings) rather than the straight line's. The course flown is     \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 327 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  solved later, after undocking and clearing: `Space::CruiseTravel::Start` runs the same check        \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 328 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  from the ship's own place and step, and flies and saves the course it settles, so a load            \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 329 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  continues it without checking again. The minutes spent clearing move the bodies little, but the     \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 330 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  course may still differ: where Start's settled driven metres exceed those paid for, the extra is    \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 331 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  burnt from the fuel aboard, and where that is short of the extra plus the fuel margin the cruise    \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 332 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  is refused (`Failure::CruiseRefused`, as today when a cruise cannot start).                         \r\u001b[7C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[2m33\u001b[12G\u001b[22m-\u001b[14G**Two\u001b[20Gclearances.**\u001b[34G`Space::CruiseDrive`\u001b[55Gand\u001b[59G`Space::Cruising`\u001b[77Gsplit\u001b[83G`clearance`\u001b[95Ginto\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 334 \u001b[22m   `departureClearance` and `arrivalClearance`, which `travel` writes as it writes the flown\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 335 \u001b[22m   profile. The hauler's stay its 1,000 km. `Policy::EstimateRoute` takes both.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mRead \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m file \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B                                         \u001b[76G\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
[0.355, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 157 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mthe magazine's next refuel needs before it sizes a cargo. \u001b[48;2;4;71;0mCargo\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m \u001b[48;2;4;71;0malready\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m \u001b[48;2;4;71;0maboard\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m \u001b[48;2;4;71;0mcan\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m still\u001b[48;2;4;71;0m fill it:\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m     \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 158 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242munsold totes from a partial sale are loaded back, so the policy's estimate (`Policy::EstimateRoute`)  \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 159 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mcounts a leg's refuel only as far as it fits, the pellets aboard plus the room the magazine has or    \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 160 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mthe totes the hold can then take, after the cargo the ship carries out of that venue, whichever is    \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 161 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mless, not a full magazine wherever pellets are sold. The starter's 12.5 kg magazine still takes one   \r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m162\u001b[12G\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mtote.    \u001b[22G  \u001b[25G  \u001b[28G          \u001b[39G        \u001b[48G    \u001b[53G   \u001b[57G     \u001b[63G  \u001b[66G  \u001b[69G      \u001b[76G   \u001b[80G        \u001b[89G       \u001b[97G    \u001b[102G   \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[2m 163 \u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 164 \u001b[22m **Units and kilograms.** A magazine, a burn and a job's fuel stay in kilograms (`World::Fuel`,\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 165 \u001b[22m `Job::pelletKilograms`); a fuel item's traded unit is converted at its kilograms a unit, from its\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;78;186;101m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39m\u001b[1mUpdate\u001b[22m(~/projects/manifest.lane-c/docs/ships-plan.md)\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  \u001b[39mAdded \u001b[1m9\u001b[22m lines\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 321 \u001b[22m   crossings are relative to the course's carrier, the star between planets, which leaves a\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 322 \u001b[22m   planet's ship behind as it orbits on (about 250,000 km in the 2.3 hours); the hauler's 1,000 km\u001b[K\r\u001b[7C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m2\u001b[12G\u001b[22m \u001b[14Gcrossing \u001b[24Gnd it\u001b[30G course move to these frames\u001b[59Gtoo, and the W22a\u001b[77Gfixtures' pins move with\u001b[102Git.\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 324 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m- **Where it is settled.** `travel` runs the check as it admits the journey, docked, from the         \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 325 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  station's place at that step, to refuse early and to burn fuel for the settled course's driven      \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 326 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  metres (its length less the two crossings) rather than the straight line's. The course flown is     \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 327 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  solved later, after undocking and clearing: `Space::CruiseTravel::Start` runs the same check        \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 328 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  from the ship's own place and ste\u001b[76Gurse it settles, so a load            \u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
