[0.210, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;78;186;101m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39m\u001b[1mUpdate\u001b[22m(~/projects/manifest.lane-c/docs/ships-plan.md)\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  \u001b[39mAdded \u001b[1m9\u001b[22m lines\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 321 \u001b[22m   crossings are relative to the course's carrier, the star between planets, which leaves a\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 322 \u001b[22m   planet's ship behind as it orbits on (about 250,000 km in the 2.3 hours); the hauler's 1,000 km\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 323 \u001b[22m   crossing and its course move to these frames too, and the W22a fixtures' pins move with it.\u001b[K\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m324\u001b[12G\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m- **Where\u001b[22Git\u001b[25Gis\u001b[28Gsettled.**\u001b[39G`travel`\u001b[48Gruns\u001b[53Gthe\u001b[57Gcheck\u001b[63Gas\u001b[66Git\u001b[69Gadmits\u001b[76Gthe\u001b[80Gjourney,\u001b[89Gdocked,\u001b[97Gfrom\u001b[102Gthe\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 325 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  station's place at that step, to refuse early and to burn fuel for the settled course's driven      \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 326 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  metres (its length less the two crossings) rather than the straight line's. The course flown is     \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 327 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  solved later, after undocking and clearing: `Space::CruiseTravel::Start` runs the same check        \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 328 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  from the ship's own place and step, and flies and saves the course it settles, so a load            \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 329 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  continues it without checking again. The minutes spent clearing move the bodies little, but the     \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 330 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  course may still differ: where Start's settled driven metres exceed those paid for, the extra is    \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 331 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  burnt from the fuel aboard, and where that is short of the extra plus the fuel margin the cruise    \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 332 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  is refused (`Failure::CruiseRefused`, as today when a cruise cannot start).                         \r\u001b[7C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[2m3\u001b[12G\u001b[22m-\u001b[14G**Two cle\u001b[24Grance\u001b[30G.** `Space::CruiseDrive` and\u001b[59G`Space::Cruising`\u001b[77Gsplit `clearance` into\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 334 \u001b[22m   `departureClearance` and `arrivalClearance`, which `travel` writes as it writes the flown\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 335 \u001b[22m   profile. The hauler's stay its 1,000 km. `Policy::EstimateRoute` takes both.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mRead \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m file \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B                                         \u001b[76G\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
